	<xs:complexType name="Component">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:appinfo>SDScomBau</xs:appinfo>
			<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
			<xs:documentation>Part or section 3, which references other sections of the component SDS.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="1" name="Substance" type="eSDScom:Substance"/>
			<!-- Was HazardIdentification -->
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="1" name="Concentration" type="eSDScom:NumericRangeWithUnitAndQualifier">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>SDScomBau</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation> Concentration: The concentration of the component in a mixture. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="AdditionalInfo" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Relevant information on the component that is not presented elsewhere. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ExposureControlPersonalProtection" type="eSDScom:BaseExposureControlPersonalProtection">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Exposure control and personal protection, information on the component: This section shall describe the applicable occupational exposure limits and necessary risk management measures. Where a chemical safety report is required, the information in this section shall be consistent with the chemical safety report and the exposure scenarios showing control of risk from the chemical safety report set out in the annex to the safety data sheet. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="PhysicalChemicalProperties" type="eSDScom:BasePhysicalChemicalProperties">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Physical and chemical properties of the component: This section of the safety data sheet shall describe the empirical data relating to the substance or mixture, if relevant. In the case of a mixture, the entries shall clearly indicate to which substance in the mixture the data apply, unless it is valid for the whole mixture. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ToxicologicalInformation" type="eSDScom:BaseToxicologicalInformation">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation> Toxicological information on the component: </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="EcologicalInformation" type="eSDScom:BaseEcologicalInformation">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ComponentInformation">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation> Information on component: Information on the component that shall be included in the SDS for the mixture. Information may include exposure limits and other information from section 8, physical-chemical properties (section 9), toxicological information (section 11) and ecological information (section 12). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IsHazardousComponent" type="boolean">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
								<xs:documentation> There is a need for an element to state if a component shall be displayed in section 3, but users have different policies on this; some want to display hazardous as well as non-hazardous components. The default value of this element should be 'true'�. </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IncludeOccupationalExposureLimits" type="boolean">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
								<xs:documentation> The component has an occupational exposure limit: 'True' means that the actual component or designation represents an exposure limit that shall be displayed in section 8 of the SDS. This element should have the default value 'true'; the exposure limit of a component will be displayed automatically. However, if this is not a component of the chemical it shall not be displayed in section 3 – only in section 8. In such cases, the value of IsHazardousComponent should be “false”. Examples on this are Annoying dust, Oil mist, etc. </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IncludeBiologicalLimitValues" type="boolean">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
								<xs:documentation> The component has a biological limit value: 'True' means that the actual component or designation has a biological limit value and shall be displayed under section 8 of the SDS. Just a few substances have such a biological limit value; the default value for this element should be 'false'�. However, if this is not a component of the mixture it shall not be displayed in section 3; only in section 8. In such cases, the value of IncludeBiologicalLimitValues should be 'false'�. Examples on this are maximum level of lead in blood and maximum concentration of mercury in urine. The components can be lead compounds, but the limit is related to level of lead. </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IncludePhysicalValues" type="boolean">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation> Information on the component to be displayed in section 9: </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IncludeToxicologicalValues" type="boolean">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
								<xs:documentation> Information on the component to be displayed in section 11: Information on the substance’s toxicological properties to be displayed in the SDS for the mixture. Such information on components may be relevant for some components in a mixture. The default value for this element should be set to “false”. The information should be displayed in the SDS in section 11. </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IncludeEcoToxicologicalValues" type="boolean">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
								<xs:documentation> Information on the component to be displayed in section 12: Information on the substance’s ecological properties to be displayed in the SDS for the mixture. Such information may be relevant for some components in a mixture – it cannot be provided for the mixture. The default value for this element should be set to “false”. The information should be displayed in the SDS in section 12. </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="CompReasonForListed" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation> Reason for stating the component in the SDS: To describe components that do not have a classification etc. </xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element minOccurs="0" name="Function" type="eSDScom:ComponentFunctionEnum"/>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="FunctionDescription" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:appinfo>SDScomChem</xs:appinfo>
								<xs:documentation>Indicate the form (solid, liquid, gas or other descriptive terms) of the substance or mixture as supplied. May be omitted if specified in field Form. If Form is "other", put more details in this field.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="TransportInformation">
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IsDangerReleasingSubstanceImdg" type="boolean"/>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="IsDangerReleasingSubstanceIata" type="boolean"/>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute default="0" name="ComponentId" type="integer"/>
		<xs:attribute default="" name="ComponentInternalSdsId" type="eSDScom:string64"/>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ControlParameters">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="OccupationalExposureLimits">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Occupational exposure limit: Values shall be given for the country where the substance or preparation is placed on the market. Give information on currently recommended monitoring procedures. For mixtures, it is useful to provide values for those constituent substances which are required to be listed in the Safety Data Sheet. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="OccupationalExposureLimit" type="eSDScom:OccupationalExposureLimit">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>aims at the product in delivery state</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="IntendedUseOccupationalExposureLimit" type="eSDScom:OccupationalExposureLimit">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>aims at degradation product limit values during use</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="BiologicalLimitValues">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Biological limit value: aims at the product in delivery state. Information regarding biological limit values - e.g. concentration of lead in blood. Biological limits will refer to individual components, not preparations. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="BiologicalLimitValue" type="eSDScom:BiologicalLimitValue">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>aims at the product in delivery state</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="IntendedUseBiologicalLimitValue" type="eSDScom:BiologicalLimitValue">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>aims at degradation product limit values during use</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="AdditionalInfo" type="eSDScom:Phrase"/>
			<xs:element minOccurs="0" name="RegionEU" type="eSDScom:ControlParametersEU">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Region-specific information in the area of exposure controls and personal protection; jurisdiction follows from the field name.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="BaseExposureControlPersonalProtection">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Used in SDS section 8. Also used in "Component" </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="PreventiveIndustrialMedicalExaminationRequired" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether occupational medical surveillance is required; yes/no or justification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ControlParameters" type="eSDScom:ControlParameters">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Exposure limits and control parameters, e.g. occupational exposure limits, DNEL, DMEL or PNEC.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="SummaryRMMeasures">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Summary of risk management measures for safe use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="SummaryRMMeasuresMan" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Summary of worker-related risk management measures.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="SummaryRMMeasuresEnvironm" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Summary of environmental risk management measures.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="RMMControlBandingApproach">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Control-banding approach to derive risk management measures; model or category.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
							<xs:complexType>
								<xs:sequence>
									<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="Task" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
										<xs:annotation>
											<xs:documentation>Description of the task or use activity in the risk management context.</xs:documentation>
										</xs:annotation>
									</xs:element>
									<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="HazardBand" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
										<xs:annotation>
											<xs:documentation>Hazard band in the control-banding system; coded or categorised information.</xs:documentation>
										</xs:annotation>
									</xs:element>
									<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ScaleOfUse" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
										<xs:annotation>
											<xs:documentation>Scale of use or amount used; qualitative information or Menge with unit.</xs:documentation>
										</xs:annotation>
									</xs:element>
									<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="AbilityToBecomeAirborne" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
										<xs:annotation>
											<xs:documentation>Potential for release into air, e.g. dustiness or volatility; qualitative information.</xs:documentation>
										</xs:annotation>
									</xs:element>
									<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ControlApproach" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
										<xs:annotation>
											<xs:documentation>Intended control approach, e.g. general ventilation, local exhaust or closed installation.</xs:documentation>
										</xs:annotation>
									</xs:element>
									<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="AdditionalInfo" type="eSDScom:Phrase"/>
								</xs:sequence>
							</xs:complexType>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<!-- Exposure controls  -->
			<xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="ExposureControlAppropriateMeasures">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Suitable engineering, organisational and personal measures to reduce exposure.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="AppropriateEngineeringControls" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Engineering controls, e.g. closed systems, local exhaust ventilation or process ventilation.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element maxOccurs="unbounded" minOccurs="0" name="ProductRelatedMeasures" type="eSDScom:Phrase">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Product-related risk reduction measures, e.g. formulation, packaging or dosing.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
